[{:adr/consequences ["any composing actor (yukkuri's cyber/anime/truecrime/pachinko channels; future gftdcojp/etzhayyim actors wanting a soundtrack) depends on kotoba-lang/composer to construct valid ai.gftd.ongakuka.compose requests and interpret track/stem/generation responses instead of re-deriving the lexicon per actor" "the actual XRPC call to ai.gftd.ongakuka.compose/regenerate (network I/O, auth, retry) stays in the app-level actor owning deployment (yukkuri's did:web:yukkuri.gftd.ai:actor:composer) -- library performs no cross-project invoke itself, matching kotoba-lang/webrtc's host-injects-transport precedent" "intentionally schema-coupled to the ongakuka lexicon (mirrors, does not generalize to any-audio-pipeline) -- a lexicon shape change requires a matching library update; avoids speculative generality" "deps.edn: no cross-kotoba-lang deps for core namespaces; kotoba.composer.ui depends on kotoba-lang/html + kotoba-lang/css if included; :test/:lint aliases match house convention (cognitect test-runner + clj-kondo)" "does not touch yukkuri's live composer actor wiring -- adopting the library into yukkuri is a separate follow-up, not bundled here"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607031510", :adr/context "{:gap \"yukkuri's composer actor (did:web:yukkuri.gftd.ai:actor:composer) cross-invokes ai.gftd.ongakuka.compose inline; no shared reusable model of the ongakuka lexicon shapes exists outside the raw lexicon JSON, so any other composing actor (yukkuri's other 3 channels, or a future non-yukkuri actor) would re-derive it from scratch\", :precedent-and-contrast \"kotoba-lang/youtube-upload was extracted from yukkuri's upload_youtube.py for the same reuse reason, but is a live third-party API client (OAuth+HTTP), accepted as a deliberate .cljc-convention exception. ongakuka.compose is different: an in-house, already-lexicon'd XRPC surface -> models as pure records + reducer, no exception needed\", :placement-check \"ADR-2606302300 step-1 layer test, as applied in kotoba-lang/webrtc (ADR-2607011700): EDN records + pure state-transition reducer, zero network I/O, zero vendor SDK -> kotoba-lang; the actual XRPC call stays with the app-level actor that owns deployment\", :naming-collision-warning \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.compose's OWN internal pipeline already has a stage called 'composer' (lyricist->composer->vocalist‖arranger->mixer->critic). kotoba-lang/composer models the OUTER request/track/stem/generation contract, not that one inner stage -- same same-word-different-referent trap as provisioning(IAM) vs provisions(contract clause) from this session's NIST CSF glossary work\"}", :adr/addendum-2026-07-07 "{:landed \"kotoba-lang/composer created + registered (repos.edn :extra-projects, west pin server-verified). core namespaces implemented: composer/track/stem/style/generation/pipeline, matching design 1:1\", :tests \"22 tests / 140 assertions, 0 failures; clj-kondo 0 warnings; CI green\", :deferred [:kotoba.composer.ui :kotoba.composer.export \"yukkuri actor adoption -- per this ADR's own P0/P1/P2 staging\"]}", :adr/decision "{:repo \"kotoba-lang/composer\", :style \"records mirror the ai.gftd.ongakuka.* lexicon 1:1 (compose/track/stem/style/generation), same rationale as kotoba-lang/webrtc mirroring RFC 8445/8866 shapes\", :namespaces {:kotoba.composer {:record \"compose-request: title, lyrics(required), style(required), style-ref-uri, language, bpm, duration-sec(5-600 default 90), model-id, seed, stems?\", :mirrors \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.compose input schema\", :features [:construct :validate]}, :kotoba.composer.track {:record \"title, lyrics, style, style-ref-uri, language(BCP-47), bpm(30-300), duration-sec(5-600), status, blob-key, mime-type, project-id, model-id, seed, created-at\", :mirrors \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.track\"}, :kotoba.composer.stem {:record \"track-uri, kind, blob-key, mime-type, duration-sec, loudness-lufs, actor-did, created-at\", :kind-enum [:vocal :chorus :drums :bass :guitar :keys :synth :strings :fx :other :instrumental :fullmix], :mirrors \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.stem\"}, :kotoba.composer.style {:record \"name, kind(:prompt|:embedding), prompt, embedding-blob-key, embedding-dim, embedding-model, license(:permissive|:own|:licensed|:unknown)\", :validator \"reject publishing an :unknown-license embedding as a record (copyright invariant from ai.gftd.ongakuka.style + yukkuri CLAUDE.md BGM/SFX license gate)\", :mirrors \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.style\"}, :kotoba.composer.generation {:record \"target-uri, stage(:lyric|:compose|:vocal|:arrange|:mix|:review|:regenerate), actor-did, model-id, params, prompt-tokens, completion-tokens, audio-sec, inference-ms, credits-consumer, credits-operator, node, status(:ok|:rejected|:failed), reject-reason, created-at\", :mirrors \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.generation\", :note \"consistent audit/metering shape any composing actor emits into\"}, :kotoba.composer.pipeline {:pattern \"pure status-transition reducer, host-injected effects (same separation of concerns as kotoba.webrtc.session)\", :states [:queued :lyric :compose :vocal :mix :review :published :rejected :failed], :mirrors \"ai.gftd.ongakuka.track status enum + ongakuka's own lyricist->composer->vocalist‖arranger->mixer->critic staging\", :effects [:request-lyrics :request-composition :request-vocal :request-arrangement :request-mix :request-review], :fn \"apply-event: track x event -> {:track next-track :effects [...]}\"}, :kotoba.composer.ui {:deps [:kotoba-lang/html :kotoba-lang/css], :note \"read-only operator dashboard, matches phone/banking/card/swift/webrtc house pattern; optional, deferrable\"}, :kotoba.composer.export {:formats [:csv :json], :note \"matches phone/banking/card/swift/webrtc house pattern; optional, deferrable\"}}}", :adr/date "2026-07-03", :db/id -1, :adr/title "kotoba-lang/composer: AI music composition request/pipeline as pure data contracts"}]